id: decisions/029-handoff-is-dated
title: "Even the agent handoff is a dated record"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'record-mutability'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: record-mutability
axis_gloss: "whether a record is corrected by appending a new entry, or by overwriting, rewriting or deleting the old one"
poles:
  a: append-only-immutable
  b: destructive-in-place-update
split: lone-exception
draft_status: full
leverage: 9.6
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(20) x split_weight(0.4) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  Is every record corrected by adding to it, with both versions kept visible —
  including the agent handoff, which today carries only an updated date and
  nothing that says when it began?

why_it_matters: >
  Append-only is the repo's most reinforced written rule (state is a reduction
  over an append-only log; corrections are new entries; branch and keep both
  visible), and the grandfather ledgers in tests/ are built the same way, may
  only shrink. Once answered, a bot handing work to the next session knows
  whether the handoff it writes is history that will be replayed or a scratch
  pointer it may overwrite.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    19 judgments sit at append-only-immutable (11 authored) and 1 at
    destructive-in-place-update (0 authored). The repository asserts both
    directions on this axis.
  attributed_to: TAXONOMY.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether Dave means the handoff to be a durable record at all, or a per-session
    scratch note that should not be in the tree.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      rule: Every record, templates included, carries a creation-time field
      (created:, timestamp: or date:) and is corrected by appending or branching,
      never by overwriting the only copy. templates/agent-handoff.yawn gains
      created: beside updated: and a supersedes: pointer to the handoff it replaces.
    cost: "Two lines in one template; existing handoffs, if any, gain created: on next touch."
    risk: "None visible; a handoff that is overwritten is still recoverable from git, so the cost of the rule is only the extra field."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Extend tests/record-shape.test.mjs (in-flight, uncommitted): every template registered as shape header must carry created:, timestamp: or date:; today templates/agent-handoff.yawn fails."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0020"
      - "J0078"
      - "J0082"
      - "J0127"
      - "J0182"
      - "J0204"
  - name: B
    description: >
      rule: Records may be edited in place; git is the only history. No record needs
      a creation field and corrections may overwrite.
    cost: "Contradicts core/state.yawn substrate.history_is_append_only: true and core/design-principles.yawn 'branch a record and keep both versions visible'; the filesystem_affordances list in core/yawn-space.yawn would need edit, overwrite and delete added."
    risk: "A replayed state can no longer be reconstructed from the records alone, which yawn.yawn canonical_sentence promises."
    reversibility: false
    proof_needed: "None can enforce this; the record would be flipping history_is_append_only to false in core/state.yawn."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0885"
  - name: C
    description: >
      rule: Every record is append-only EXCEPT a record declared mutability:
      current-state-pointer, which is a View over history (a reduction, not an
      event) and may be overwritten; its history lives in git and it may never be
      cited as proof. templates/agent-handoff.yawn is the one template declared this
      way and says so in a mutability: line.
    cost: "One line in the template, one sentence in core/state.yawn distinguishing an event from a pointer."
    risk: "A second template declares itself a pointer to escape the rule."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Extend tests/record-shape.test.mjs: a header template without a creation field must carry mutability: current-state-pointer, and scripts/validate-proof-refs.mjs must reject a proof.source pointing at a record carrying that line."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0078"
      - "J0127"
      - "J0885"

recommendation:
  option_ref: A
  confidence: 0.7
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    Eleven authored judgments and the substrate contract sit on append-only; the
    one exception is a revealed reading of a missing field, with no sentence
    anywhere saying the handoff is meant to be mutable. Removing the exception
    costs two lines; writing it down (C) would introduce a new record class the
    constitution does not have. If Dave does intend the handoff as a scratch
    pointer, C is the honest version, but nothing in the tree says so today.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "templates/agent-handoff.yawn carries created: and supersedes: beside updated:."
    - "A test in tests/ rejects a header-shape template without a creation-time field and passes."
    - "core/yawn-space.yawn filesystem_affordances still lists no edit, overwrite or delete verb."

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A record in records/ is changed in place with its earlier content gone from
    the tree and no receipt or branch names the change, while the tests stay
    green.
  status: proposed

evidence_sample:
  - "J0020"
  - "J0078"
  - "J0082"
  - "J0127"
  - "J0182"
  - "J0204"
  - "J0885"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
  id_index: TAXONOMY.md
